{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-331954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-{45}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=b+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{72}^{∘}).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-331954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-{45}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 5x-{45}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & ={30}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={150}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 5x & ={75}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={195}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={39}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b={39}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-331954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-331954" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-331954" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "39"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-16252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{25}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n,\\,x=b+{120}^{∘}n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-16252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+{30}^{∘} & =-{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n, & \\, & \\, & 3x+{30}^{∘} & =-{135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-{30}^{∘}-{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 3x & =-{30}^{∘}-{135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ 3x & =-{75}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 3x & =-{165}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ x & =-{25}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & x & =-{55}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=-{55}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-16252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-16252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-16252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{105}^{∘}"] ["math" "-{165}^{∘}"] ["math" "-{35}^{∘}"] ["math" "-{45}^{∘}"] ["math" "-{55}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-16252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{55}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-65848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=b\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-65848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & x+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-65848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-65848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-65848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-65848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-274647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=\\pi +2\\pi n,\\,x=b\\pi +2\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[0,2).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-274647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{6\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\pi +2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-274647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-274647" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-274647" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-327876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{60}^{∘})=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=b+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={195}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-327876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{60}^{∘} & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x-{60}^{∘} & ={330}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={210}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={330}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & ={270}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={390}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={135}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={195}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b={135}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-327876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-327876" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-327876" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "135"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx={720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2}+{150}^{∘} & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={150}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & ={210}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & ={360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & ={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={720}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={120}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={120}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-328241" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328241" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "120"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-330218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{120}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-330218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{120}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{120}^{∘} & ={330}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={30}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={330}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & =-{90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={210}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & =-{45}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={105}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={105}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-330218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-330218" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-330218" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "105"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-19756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=\\pi a+\\pi n\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-19756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4} & =0+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{8}+\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-\\frac{3}{8}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-19756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-19756" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff