nd{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={85}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328240" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-328240" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328240" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "85"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{125}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{40}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{125}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{125}^{∘} & ={315}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={315}^{∘}-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & =-{80}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={190}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & =-{40}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={95}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={95}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-328237" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328237" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "95"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{24}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{12}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-42800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{10}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{12}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{24}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x+{30}^{∘})=0\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+n\\cdot {45}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{45}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+{30}^{∘})=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+{30}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={90}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 4x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+n\\cdot {45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={15}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-328425" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328425" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $n$ is any integer. What could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{9}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{9}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha25