on" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{30}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={75}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={37.5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=37.5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-328250" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328250" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "37.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +2n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,2).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=\\frac{1}{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-328434" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328434" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3x)=-2\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3},\\,x=a\\pi +\\frac{2\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,\\frac{2}{3}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n3x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n,\\,3x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n, & \\,3x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}, & \\,x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{9}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{4}{9}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-328452" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-328452" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘})=2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=1\\,{120}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘}={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,\\frac{x}{4}+{20}^{∘}={300}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4}=-{20}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{4}=-{20}^{∘}+{300}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ \\frac{x}{4}={40}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{4}={280}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x={160}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,x=1\\,{120}^{∘}+1\\,{440}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=160.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-42788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "110"] ["math" "160"] ["math" "210"] ["math" "240"] ["math" "80"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "160"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(5x)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5},\\,x=a+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n5x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n,\\,5x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n, & \\,5x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5}, & \\,x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{30}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{7\\pi }{30}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-121076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{6\\pi }{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{7\\pi }{30}"] ["math" "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi }{30}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x=-2\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+\\pi n,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}+n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+n\\pi \\,\\,\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-42789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{7\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-42789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi }{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=-2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={480}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}={120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,\\frac{x}{2}={240}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,\\frac{x}{2} & ={240}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={240}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,x & ={480}^{∘}+{720}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=240.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "998d0e47ab9e2bb3a2e68d7a135a6c3172c7dc80cd219aae997121c292bf1093"} {"question" "q-121068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "120"] ["math" "240"] ["math" "270"] ["math" "300"] ["math" "360"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "q-121068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "240"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/state.json" "file_sha256" "430c88ff3e1d422ed9988c4787a375b259fdc37a4fbe642ddbac0d0c220d9653"} {"question" "e-3779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(4x-90^\\circ\\right)} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-3779.json" "file_sha256" "9d01b9bbd16e1661bc0d040544efff131c40fdf9af1a24026441edd5e91c5fb6"} {"question" "e-3779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n, & \\, & \\, & 4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={90}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & ={90}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ 4x & ={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & =-{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & x & =-{15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-3779.json" "file_sha256" "9d01b9bbd16e1661bc0d040544efff131c40fdf9af1a24026441edd5e91c5fb6"} {"question" "e-8659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\cos \\left(6x + 75^\\circ \\right) = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-8659.json" "file_sha256" "1a39a2e88999c53ba0156f0cf38d25ca0822cede523fa3dfe4339644e0d3154d"} {"question" "e-8659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+{75}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 6x+{75}^{∘} & ={225}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 6x & ={150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={25}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-8659.json" "file_sha256" "1a39a2e88999c53ba0156f0cf38d25ca0822cede523fa3dfe4339644e0d3154d"} {"question" "e-3780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(2x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\right) =  -1\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-3780.json" "file_sha256" "e925a9892070feeac8f8dcee778a92f106bdbd16c16e130841daaa6a995f434e"} {"question" "e-3780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-3780.json" "file_sha256" "e925a9892070feeac8f8dcee778a92f106bdbd16c16e130841daaa6a995f434e"} {"question" "e-3781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\sec\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-3781.json" "file_sha256" "49ea9e34ac6899664730aa1d64725feeb7cd49b926d3c37276060b3a55326658"} {"question" "e-3781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n, \\qquad\\qquad 2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x=-\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x=\\frac{5\\pi }{8}+\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-3781.json" "file_sha256" "49ea9e34ac6899664730aa1d64725feeb7cd49b926d3c37276060b3a55326658"}] "usage" {"e-3779" [] "q-42788" [] "q-42789" [] "e-3780" [] "e-8659" [] "e-3781" []} "basis" 844 "retractions" [[17592186101320 :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\sec (\\frac{x}{4} + 20^{∘}) = 2$.\nThe general solution of this equation is\n$x = a^{∘} + 1440^{∘} \\cdot n, x = 1120^{∘} + 1440^{∘} \\cdot n$,\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a$?"] [17592186101321 :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\csc 2x =-2$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n$x = a + πn, x = \\frac{11π}{12} + πn$,\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a$?"] [17592186100578 :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$\\sin{\\left(4x-90^\\circ\\right)} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}$"] [17592186100578 :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x - 90^{∘} &= -30^{∘} + 360^{∘}n, \\mid 4x - 90^{∘}|=-150^{∘} + 360^{∘}n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}4x &= 90^{∘} - 30^{∘} + 360^{∘}n & 4x|= 90^{∘} - 150^{∘} + 360^{∘}n \\\\ 4x|= 60^{∘} + 360^{∘}n & 4x|=-60^{∘} + 360^{∘}n \\\\ x|= 15^{∘} + 90^{∘}n & x|=-15^{∘} + 90^{∘}n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186100707 :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\cos \\left(6x + 75^\\circ \\right) = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$"] [17592186100707 :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 75^{∘} &= 135^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}, \\mid 6x + 75^{∘}|= 225^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}6x &= 60^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘} & 6x|= 150^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘} \\\\ x|= 10^{∘} + n \\cdot 60^{∘} & x|= 25^{∘} + n \\cdot 60^{∘}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186100579 :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\tan\\left(2x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = -1$"] [17592186100579 :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - \\frac{π}{4} &= -\\frac{π}{4} + nπ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x &= nπ \\\\\nx &= \\frac{nπ}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186100580 :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n$\\sec\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{2}$"] [17592186100580 :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n, \\qquad\\qquad 2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x =-\\frac{π}{2} + \\frac{π}{4} + 2πn, & 2x =-\\frac{π}{2} + \\frac{7π}{4} + 2πn \\\\ 2x =-\\frac{π}{4} + 2πn, & 2x = \\frac{5π}{4} + 2πn \\\\ x =-\\frac{π}{8} + πn, & x = \\frac{5π}{8} + πn\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186099517 17592186099518 17592186099519 17592186099520 17592186099521 17592186099523 17592186099524 17592186099525 17592186099526 17592186099527] "immutable_fields" [[17592186099516 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099516 :answer-field/id] [17592186099516 :answer-field/key] [17592186099516 :answer-field/type] [17592186099522 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099522 :answer-field/id] [17592186099522 :answer-field/key] [17592186099522 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
